uestion.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c9e4a51-c450-52e6-9d4d-f69fe8fdfc95" :question/math-academy-id "q-102673" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $C={A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $C={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a10723d3-f77a-5b16-956e-675d06c9d2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461219} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b5ac11-5a94-5e5a-a683-6eaa4e645176" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461220}] :answer-field/corre